  "brief": "Altria is reportedly considering a $30B takeover bid for Imperial Brands, with the deal's stage currently shrouded in mystery.\n\nAltria / Imperial Brands (Rumored): Altria to Buy Imperial Brands. Altria is considering a $30B takeover bid for Imperial Brands [1, 4, 5]. Altria has until Christmas Eve to bid for Imperial Brands worth $34B [2, 3]. Altria's bid for Imperial Brands is reportedly worth £26bn [3, 6]. Altria is exploring a takeover bid for Imperial Brands [7, 8].\nCrowdStrike / Zscaler (Announced): CrowdStrike and Zscaler Deal. CrowdStrike is acquiring Zscaler in an all-stock deal [13, 14, 19]. The deal was initially valued at $32 billion [15]. The deal was later revised to $43.9 billion [16, 17]. The deal was announced on November 23 [15, 16, 17].\nTarga / Kinetik (Rumored): Targa and Kinetik Deal Rumors. Targa is in talks to acquire Kinetik, a Permian pipeline operator [23, 24, 25]. The deal is reportedly a major pipeline tie-up [26, 27]. The stage of the deal is currently rumored [21, 22, 26].\nVerizon / Fidium (Rumored): Verizon to Buy Fidium. Verizon is in talks to buy Fidium for $6 billion [28, 29, 30]. The deal is still in its early stages and no official announcement has been made [28, 29, 30].\nSlate Medicines / Fulcrum Therapeutics (Announced): Slate Medicines and Fulcrum Therapeutics Merger. Slate Medicines and Fulcrum Therapeutics are merging [31, 32]. The merger is announced [31, 32]. No further information is available [31, 32].\nMDA SPACE / BLUE CANYON TECHNOLOGIES (Completed): MDA SPACE ACQUIRES BLUE CANYON TECHNOLOGIES. MDA SPACE has acquired BLUE CANYON TECHNOLOGIES [33, 34]. The deal is now completed [33, 34].\nUber / Delivery Hero (Announced): Uber to Acquire Delivery Hero. Uber is acquiring Delivery Hero [35, 36]. The deal has cleared a key shareholder hurdle [35]. Uber has secured 87.13% of Delivery Hero shares [36].\nCanadian Natural / Big Advantage Energy (Announced): Canadian Natural to Acquire Advantage Energy. Canadian Natural is acquiring Advantage Energy in a $1.8-billion deal [38, 39]. A shareholder of Big Advantage Energy opposes the $2.5B takeover bid [37]. The deal was announced [37, 38, 39].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Puig agrees to buy 75% stake in perfume group Artessence in deal valuing it at $1.9 billion [40].\n- Armani heirs consider buying small slice of fashion house in stake sale, sources say [41].\n- Fulcrum estimates a cash dividend of up to about $3.61 per share; the final payment may differ [42].",
